      "files": {
        "0": {
          "id": "0",
          "name": "main.py",
          "language": "py",
          "contents": "# CIW AI Associate Standard: 3.12\n# Standard Description: Explain the major distinctions between algorithms to fit supervised and unsupervised models.\n#\n# Rationale: While both Supervised and Unsupervised models use a .fit() method \n# in scikit-learn, what happens \"under the hood\" is very different. \n# - Supervised Fit: Minimizes the ERROR between its guess and the real label.\n# - Unsupervised Fit: Minimizes the DISTANCE between points to find clusters.\n# This tutorial compares the internal logic of these two \"Fitting\" processes.\n\n\"\"\"\nWelcome! Today we're looking at the difference between \"Learning with a Key\" \nand \"Learning by Looking\".\n\nThink of it like a puzzle:\n- Supervised: You have the picture on the box (the labels) to help you.\n- Unsupervised: You have no picture—you just group the blue pieces together \n  and the green pieces together.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression\nfrom sklearn.cluster import KMeans\nimport numpy as np\n\n# --- THE DATA ---\n# X is the input (Features), y is the \"Answer Key\" (Labels)\nX = np.array([[1], [2], [10], [11]])\ny = np.array([5, 10, 50, 55]) # y = x * 5 (approx)\n\n# --- PART 1: SUPERVISED FITTING ---\nprint(\"--- Part 1: Supervised Fitting (Learning the Key) ---\")\n# The algorithm looks at X AND y. \n# It tries to find a formula: y = (X * weight) + intercept\nsup_model = LinearRegression()\nsup_model.fit(X, y) # Notice we pass BOTH X and y\n\nprint(f\"Supervised rule found: Multiply by {sup_model.coef_[0]:.1f}\")\n\n# --- PART 2: UNSUPERVISED FITTING ---\nprint(\"\\n--- Part 2: Unsupervised Fitting (Finding Groups) ---\")\n# The algorithm ONLY looks at X. \n# It doesn't know about 'y'. It just sees that 1 and 2 are close together, \n# and 10 and 11 are close together.\nunsup_model = KMeans(n_clusters=2, n_init=10)\nunsup_model.fit(X) # Notice we ONLY pass X!\n\n# It doesn't find a formula; it finds \"Centers\".\nprint(f\"Unsupervised centers found at: {unsup_model.cluster_centers_.flatten()}\")\n\n\"\"\"\n--- YOUR TURN ---\nWe've listed three algorithms below. \n1. Determine if each one requires a 'y' (the labels) to fit.\n2. If it does, it's Supervised. If not, it's Unsupervised.\n\n- Algorithm A: LogisticRegression\n- Algorithm B: PCA (Principal Component Analysis)\n- Algorithm C: RandomForestClassifier\n\"\"\"\n\n# STARTING CODE FOR STUDENT:\n# TODO: Match the styles!\n# Alg_A = \"___\"\n# Alg_B = \"___\"\n# Alg_C = \"___\"\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": true
